---
description: ITW release versions — each dotted slot is a single digit 0-9
alwaysApply: true
---

# ITW version slots are single digits

IcedTea-Web `release_version`, tags, release branches, and package names use dotted integers. **Every slot is one decimal digit (0–9). Never 10 or higher in any slot.**

When the last slot is already `9`, increment the previous slot and reset the rest to `0`.

```text
# ✅ GOOD
3.1.9 → next is 3.2.0
3.2.0 → 3.2.1 → … → 3.2.9 → 3.3.0
3.9.9 → 4.0.0
icedtea-web-3.2.0
release/icedtea-web-3.2.0

# ❌ BAD — two-digit slot
3.1.10
3.0.10
2.9.10
icedtea-web-3.1.10
```

Do not dispatch, tag, or name an MSI/ZIP with a two-digit slot. If a draft like `3.1.10` already exists, skip it and use the next legal version (`3.2.0`).
